@author "Claude (Anthropic)"

; fish-base vertex: O = incenter of triangle abd, a point ON the ac-diagonal.
; All three given rays are bare, hence unconstrained, so the solution space
; covers the M/V pattern and the stacking as well as the emergent ray's
; position. The POSITION is
; forced regardless (the diagonal's OppositeRay continuation O -> c; both
; line-new candidates fold a flap off the paper for every Maekawa pattern),
; the min-mountain canon then narrows to 3 patterns, and `(toward)`'s
; rank-dipole stage picks among THOSE by which side's material ends up on
; top. `(toward .b)` (this file) and its sibling `(toward .d)` therefore
; pick the two MIRROR realizations: same face count, same table positions,
; opposite layer order: two different folds.
;
; `.bel` assertions have no vocabulary for the layer order (see
; tests/test_bel_assert.ml's `assertion` type), so `faces = 6` is all this
; file can pin; the DIFFERENCE (this file's layer order vs. -toward-d.bel's)
; is pinned by tests/test_flatten.ml's
; test_flatten_derive_opposite_ray_fish_base, which reads Fold_state.order
; directly and asserts the two runs disagree.

paper square

mark (map .a onto .c) as --diag
mark (through .a .c) as --ray

mark (map --ab onto --diag) as --l1
mark (map --da onto --diag) as --l2
flatten (--l1 valley) (--l2 valley) (--ray & .a valley) (staying .c) (toward .b)

; assert faces = 6
